<title>JAPAN: Swedish Export launches 15 bln yen dual samurais.</title>
<headline>Swedish Export launches 15 bln yen dual samurais.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Export Credit Corp (SEK) on Monday launched 15 billion yen worth of 5.8 percent yen/Australian dollar dual currency samurai bonds due on October 28, 1999, lead manager Kankaku Securities said.</p>
<p>The bonds are priced at par.</p>
<p>Holders of the samurai bonds will receive A$1,138.77 for each 100,000-yen bond held at maturity and A$11,387.70 for each one-million-yen bond.</p>
<p>The coupon will be paid in yen, while redemption will be in Australian dollars.  </p>
<p>The breakdown of the terms is as follows:</p>
<p>AMT 15 bln yen	COUPON 5.8 pct    MATURITY Oct 28, 1999</p>
<p>TYPE yen/A$ samurai ISS PRICE 100 yen PAY DATE Oct 28, 1996</p>
<p>SUB PERIOD Oct 4 to Oct 23</p>
<p>INTEREST PAYMENT April 28 and Oct 28</p>
<p>SIGN DATE Oct 3</p>
<p>LAST RATING AA+(S&amp;P), Aa3(Moody's)</p>
<p>LEAD MANAGER Kankaku Securities</p>
<p>LEAD TRUSTEE Dai-Ichi Kangyo Bank</p>
</text>
